        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "bd3fb30e85425ccc",
      "line_num": 201,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Obsidian Markdown Emitter v1 (Description + Siblings + MOC) (2026-05-02): Three Phase 3 enrichments shipped. (1) Description \u2014 `_python_metadata` and `_node_metadata` now capture the manifest's `description` field and `emit_markdown` renders it as a paragraph between H1 and bullets, giving each note real human-readable context. (2) Sibling wikilinks \u2014 new `_compute_siblings(projects, filenames)` groups by parent directory; each project gets a `- Siblings: [[a]], [[b]]` bullet linking to others in the same parent, so Obsidian draws real graph edges between sibling notes. (3) MOC \u2014 new `_write_moc` emits an `Index.md` at the vault root with all 180 projects grouped by parent directory under `## <parent>` headings, hub-and-spoke from a single index node. Verified end-to-end on `~`: project_finder shows its description and 13 sibling links to other `~/bin/` repos; Index.md groups across 45 parent dirs. Three follow-ups filed (per-note Structure section, incremental-scan v2 for sibling/desc changes, shared-dep wikilinks).**\n- [x] Description from manifest, rendered between H1 and bullets\n- [x] Sibling wikilinks via `_compute_siblings`\n- [x] `Index.md` MOC via `_write_moc`\n- [x] Re-scanned `~` end-to-end and confirmed all three render\n\n`TODO.md:L201`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 240
    },
    {
      "children": [
